  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the PO, I want the survey to ask about the options now kept behind **Réglages › Expérimental** (#903), and the D1 question to show its section cards, so that the answers tell us which experimental options members want by default, and iPad/Duo respondents see what each section is. (Operator, 2026-11-15.) Content only: the form's architecture stays as built in #712.\n\n### 1. One new question on the experimental options\n\nThe wording must stay as short and light as the existing questions (`docs/ux/questionnaire/questions.md`). Proposed:\n\n### X1\n- Section du tri : (nouvelle, options expérimentales, #903)\n- Question : Ces options sont en test dans l'app. Lesquelles voulez-vous par défaut ?\n- Réponses (plusieurs choix) : `composer_moderne` Zone de réponse compacte, collée au clavier · `recherche_barre` Recherche dans la barre du bas · `lignes_icones` Icônes de drapeau devant le titre · `stockage_mp_detaille` Stockage MP réglable par fonction · `choix_images` Choix du chargement des images · `aucune` Aucune, garder l'app comme aujourd'hui\n- Aide : « Cochez celles que vous aimeriez voir activées pour tous. »\n- Condition : (aucune)\n\nRules:\n- `aucune` excludes the other answers.\n- No visual is required. If a capture of an option exists later, it is added under the same naming rules as `visuels/`.\n- Place X1 right after the L/D blocks, before the closing questions. Its position follows `cadrage-construction.md` §2.\n\n### 2. D1 section cards (PO go, 2026-11-15)\n\n- The D1 cards exist since #914: `docs/ux/questionnaire/visuels/scenarios/D1-cartes/*.png`. Show them in the D1 question (iPad and Duo unfolded path): one card per section, next to its state (garder / déplier / écarter), and keep the sort.\n- This is point 2 of « Écarts avec la consigne » in #914, now decided.\n- Change only what the cards need (`app.js`, its tests). The CSP and the « no resource from another domain » rule are unchanged, because the cards are served by the binary.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- French. The wording and the answer ids follow the existing style. No proposal the PO classed **Non** (§3.5).\n- Update together:\n  - `questions.md`;\n  - the form's question data;\n  - the concordance test;\n  - the JS tests;\n  - `donnees.md` if the new answers change what is stored. They are choice ids only, with no free text.\n- `go test ./...`, `node --test` and markdownlint stay green, and the `ux-survey` workflow passes.\n\n### Order\n\nThis lands **before** UX-11 (#635), so the security review covers the final form once.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] X1 is in `questions.md` and in the form, with `aucune` exclusive, and a concordance test covers it.\n- [ ] D1 shows its 9 cards on the iPad/Duo path; tests cover their display and order.\n- [ ] All the survey checks are green.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
